# __PROJECT__

C++__CPP_STANDARD__ project using G++, CMake 3.28+ and Ninja, with a
`libs/core` library target, a thin `app` executable, and Catch2 tests.

```bash
cmake --preset dev
cmake --build --preset dev
./build/dev/bin/__PROJECT__
ctest --preset dev --output-on-failure
```

`build/dev` carries sanitizers (`-fsanitize=address,undefined`) and debug
symbols; `build/release` is the optimized configuration with its own preset.
Configure editor diagnostics from `build/dev/compile_commands.json`.

Keep reusable logic in `libs/core`; extract a second library target once a
second consumer actually appears. The sample `core::greeting()` function and
its Catch2 case exist only to prove the scaffold builds and tests end to end —
replace them with real logic.
